    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, I'm Dr. Smith. It's nice to meet you; could you tell me what brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S014",
      "patient_response": "Nice to meet you, Dr. Smith. So, uh, I’m here because I feel like I’m just always running hot, you know? Like I can’t shut the motor off. Which is funny, because I actually love working on motors. I was helping my buddy rebuild the engine on his old Chevy truck last weekend, and man, getting that alternator bracket to line up was a total nightmare. We must have spent three hours just looking for the right size socket wrench because his garage is an absolute disaster zone. I keep telling him he needs to put up a pegboard system, but he never listens, he just leaves his tools wherever they fall. Anyway, uh... wait, where was I going with that? Oh, right. My motor. Being unable to shut it off. Yeah, so lately that whole always-being-on thing has been getting me in a lot of trouble at the firehouse, so... here I am.",
