    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "You mentioned feeling like you can't shut your motor off lately—would you say this feeling is something you've dealt with your whole life, or does it come and go in distinct episodes that are different from how you usually feel?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Man, I don't really know. I've never really thought about it like... episodes, or whatever. I guess I'm not sure if it's been forever? Like, I've just always been me, you know? But speaking of episodes, we had this absolute crazy call last Tuesday. Total chaos. This guy tried to deep fry a frozen turkey on his wooden deck, and, uh, you know how that goes. The oil just explodes everywhere. We roll up, and the whole back porch is just fully engulfed. And the guy is standing there in his flip-flops with a garden hose, which is literally the absolute worst thing you can do for a grease fire. I had to physically pull him back. I mean, water and oil, they just don't mix. It's like when I tried to make this fancy vinaigrette from scratch for my wife for our anniversary last year... I shook that mason jar for like twenty minutes and it still separated. I ended up just running to the store and buying the bottled stuff. She didn't even notice, thank god. But, uh... wait. What did you ask me? Something about how I usually feel?",
