    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Looking back over the last few years, have there been any periods of several days or weeks where you felt unusually low, sad, or hopeless?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Low, sad, or hopeless? No, I don't think so. I mean, I get bummed out sometimes, sure, but not for days or weeks at a time. Like, I was pretty annoyed last month when my favorite pizza place closed down. We used to go there every Friday after shift, you know? They had this amazing buffalo chicken slice with the perfect amount of ranch drizzled on top. Not too much ranch, just right. People always drown things in ranch, and it ruins the crust. It gets all soggy. I hate soggy pizza. Actually, that reminds me, my basement flooded a bit last spring, and getting that carpet ripped up was a nightmare. The smell alone... ugh. We had to rent one of those giant industrial fans. The guy at the rental place was super helpful, though. Showed me exactly how to set it up. He used to be a volunteer firefighter, actually, so we got to talking about gear and how heavy the new turnout coats are. But, yeah, no, I wouldn't say I get super sad or hopeless. Just... normal stuff, I guess.",
