    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Looking back at your time in elementary or middle school, did your teachers or parents ever comment on you being unable to sit still, constantly moving, or having trouble focusing on your schoolwork?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Yeah, actually, my mom says I was exactly like this back in grade school, too. Always popping out of my seat, blurting out answers before the teacher even finished asking the question, losing my homework... I swear, I used to get so many notes sent home. Which is crazy, because I was bright enough to do the work, I just... couldn't keep it together. Speaking of notes, we have this new dispatcher at the station, and she leaves these sticky notes everywhere. Like, everywhere. On the coffee maker, on the steering wheel of the rig... it's kind of driving me nuts. The other day, she left a note on the fridge saying \"Please label your tupperware,\" but she used this neon pink pen that was almost impossible to read. I mean, who uses pink pen on a yellow sticky note? It's terrible contrast. I actually took a graphic design class back when I was getting my associate's degree, and color theory was like, week one. We had this project where we had to design a logo for a fake coffee shop, and I spent way too much time trying to pick the perfect shade of brown. I think I called it \"The Daily Grind\" or something cheesy like that. I got a B on it, though. But anyway, yeah, school... I was definitely a handful back then. Always moving around.",
